<title>BELGIUM: Belgian FAFER says H1 96/97 profits down.</title>
<headline>Belgian FAFER says H1 96/97 profits down.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(figures in millions of Belgian francs)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	     111.232	vs  250.729</p>
<p>NOTE: Belgian stainless steel maker Fabrique de Fer de Charleroi said it was clear the optimism it expressed last year had failed to materialise. In fact, it said, the economy had suffered considerably during the first half of its book year which runs from July to June, and the second half would be little better.  </p>
<p>    Ind cash flow	     281.511	vs  745.536</p>
<p>    Provisions		  232.302	vs  298.030</p>
<p>    Financial results	   3.886	vs    9.999</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  83.830	vs  -10.009</p>
<p>    Tax			    25.693	vs  196.767</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
